    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2477c6ef-b876-5c1f-b42f-d37546e8cf6f",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Express $10\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{9}\\right)-5$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Collect the common factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&10\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{9}\\right)-5\\\\&=5\\left(2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{9}\\right)-1\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the alternative cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n2\\cos^2 x-1=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=\\frac{5\\pi}{9}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{9}\\right)-1&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi}{9}\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(\\frac{10\\pi}{9}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5\\left(2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{9}\\right)-1\\right)&=5\\cos\\left(\\frac{10\\pi}{9}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
