      ":question/problem": "Express $2-4\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{5}\\right)$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Collect the common factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&2-4\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{5}\\right)\\\\&=2\\left(1-2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{5}\\right)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the alternative cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n1-2\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=\\frac{3\\pi}{5}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1-2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{5}\\right)&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi}{5}\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(\\frac{6\\pi}{5}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\left(1-2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{5}\\right)\\right)&=2\\cos\\left(\\frac{6\\pi}{5}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
